results.question:
Identify the cause of an infinite re-render loop in this React component snippet:

useEffect(() => {
  fetchData().then(res => setData(res));
});

results.userAnswer:
Without a dependency array, useEffect runs after every render. Since setData(res) updates the component's state, it triggers another render, which runs the effect again, creating an infinite loop.
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData().then(res => setData(res));
}, []);

